  "findings": [
    "Raw Wikipedia contains lists, references, missing template values and extraction residue; footer/short-unit filters and defect filters remove many, at a cost to lead/context retention.",
    "Human instructions include varied classification, explanation, writing, summarization, extraction, practical advice and programming. They also contain grammar errors, unsupported assumptions and unreliable facts/code.",
    "Four versioned input-level quarantines and four output-level quarantines retain the reasons and source IDs. No answer was rewritten.",
    "The full-size post-filter sample identified unsupported C# platform claims, overbroad security claims/missing requested bullet format, an unsupported no-car assumption, and an extraction artifact; all four removed before tokenizer fitting.",
    "Multi-turn examples were inspected for actual alternating roles and follow-up coherence. Incorrect sampled code/biographical continuations were removed. Remaining turns are not certified factually consistent.",
    "Final samples retain typos, uneven concision, dated facts and confident simplifications; no factual-error rate, safety score or representative domain balance is claimed.",
    "The pretraining source is entirely encyclopedic, with sampled geography, transport, biographies, arts/media, history/law, zoology and taxonomy. It is not a balanced modern web, textbook or code corpus."
  ],
